Here are the three main things you'll do in this "early access" game, in order:
1. Pick some apples;
2. Hike across a Soviet♥♥♥♥♥♥hole for hours on end, (probably) finding nothing;
3. Die.
Running simulator, 2k17 edition.

In the span of about 8 hours Undertale has made me question many things;
It made me question my choices in life and how they affect others...
It made me question whether or not violence truly solves anything...
It made me ask whether my life is worth more to me than the lives of others...
But the most important question this game made me ask;
It made me ask whether I like butterscotch more than cinnamon.

