This game is a complete joke. I'm sure it would be developed faster if Bohemia Interactive hired a troop of monkeys and let them do the job. Early Access is a stupid idea, they got the money and now they are just hanging around, doing nothing.
Someday Half-Life 3 will come out, and on that day DayZ will still not be playable. It's so bugged it makes you want to hang yourself. I strongly advise against wasting your money on this game before it's released (if it ever comes to that).
// 21.11.2016 - it's still worthless.

A lot of DayZ reviews;
"Geeze, what are these guys doing with all the money?"
Smart people;
"Huh, they've gotten around two years of development in. They plan on beta at three years. That seems perfectly normal for a development cycle."
Ignore the reviews that say that the game devs are just wasting your money. This is much better than H1Z1, the landscapes are the most beautiful thing you'll ever see, and the end product will be the most unique experience on the market.

!WARNING. PLAY THIS GAME KNOWING NOTHING. NOTHING IS SPOILT IN THIS REVIEW! Well what to say that hasn't been said. Let's start with the positives. The game looks...odd. It has an old GB or SNES look to it, but the sprites are brilliantly done. The battle system is interesting, you could do a timed attack to harm an emeny, or you could give it a hug and ask it how its day went. Its your choice. Oh, and the fluid morality system is great. EVERYTHING you do is remembered. EVERY enemy you kill is dead. EVERY action is judged. The game constantly judges you for your actions, not in your face, but passively, until it slaps you on your first play through. If you do decide to kill every single monster...you heartless ♥♥♥♥♥♥♥ you...the game tries desperately to stop you, as the character at the end knows what will happen, what will be if you do go through. Oh and the music is stellar. Buy the f*cking soundtrack you cheapscate.
Ok now on to the only negative. Undertale has so many secrets, so many different possibilities, yet it makes you feel like an ♥♥♥♥♥♥♥ for restarting the game. Even the only truly evil character knows this, and gives you a guilt trip. He is the first character to try and almost succeed in killing you, and he gives you a guilt trip. Its masterfully done, but it really wants you to lay the game to rest and let fake, yet awesome fictional characters continue their lives.
Overall great game, great characters, writing, music, jokes, secrets, 8 dogs, and sans stop looking at me ;_;

